  "content": {
    "id": "p4-problem-2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Find the domain of $y=\\log_{10}(x)+\\log_{10}(x-2)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x>2$",
      "worked": "Both logarithm arguments must be positive.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&>0\\\\x-2&>0\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe second condition gives $x>2$, which also satisfies $x>0$. The domain is $x>2$.",
